# go-blog

A modern, dual-mode blogging platform written in **Go 1.23**.

It can be operated in two modes:
1. **Static Mode (GitHub Pages)**: Zero-server, zero-database static HTML/CSS site generated directly from Markdown files and automatically deployed via GitHub Actions.
2. **Dynamic Mode (Server + Database)**: Gin web server with MySQL database, supporting writer dashboard, admin portal, and REST APIs.

---

## Mode 1: Static Blog (GitHub Pages)

### 1. Authoring Posts
Posts are written in Markdown with YAML frontmatter in [`content/posts/`](content/posts/):

```bash
# Create a new post template
make new-post TITLE="My New Article"
# or
./bin/ssg new -title "My New Article"
```

Example markdown structure (`content/posts/my-new-article.md`):
```markdown
---
title: "My New Article"
slug: "my-new-article"
author: "Your Name"
date: "2026-09-20"
published: true
summary: "A brief preview of the post."
---

Your markdown article content here...
```

### 2. Building & Previewing Locally
```bash
# Build static site to dist/
make build-static

# Preview locally on http://localhost:3000
make serve-static
```

### 3. Deploying to GitHub Pages
A GitHub Actions workflow is included at [`.github/workflows/pages.yml`](.github/workflows/pages.yml).

To enable GitHub Pages in your repository:
1. In your GitHub repository, go to **Settings** → **Pages**.
2. Under **Build and deployment** → **Source**, select **GitHub Actions**.
3. Push changes to `main` (or commit a new post to `content/posts/`).
4. GitHub Actions will automatically compile the static site and deploy it to `https://<username>.github.io/<repo-name>/`.

---

## Mode 2: Dynamic Server (Go + MySQL)

### Running with Docker Compose
```bash
docker compose up --build
```
- Web Application: `http://localhost:8080`
- MySQL Database: `localhost:3306`

### Running Locally
```bash
cd backend
go run main.go
```

---

## Exporting MySQL Posts to Static Markdown
If you have existing posts in your MySQL database and want to convert them to static markdown files:
```bash
./bin/ssg export-db
```
This exports all database posts to `content/posts/*.md`.

---

## AI Agent Integration (ContextOS)
This repository includes ContextOS runtime integrations for **Antigravity**, **Cursor**, **Claude Code**, and **Codex**:
```bash
# Resume persistent context and latest branch state
./bin/ctx resume

# Assemble token-budgeted context for a task
./bin/ctx plan -task "Add syntax highlighting" -budget 2000

# View indexed code graph and memory stats
./bin/ctx stats
```